1
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:11,200
Are you all right, Lydia?

2
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,540
No, I’m not, Dad.

3
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:15,360
I’m not well at all.

4
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,940
What’s the matter with you?

5
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:19,920
I’ve got a really bad stomach ache.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,400
Do you think it was something you ate?

7
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:24,800
No, not just one thing.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,160
She ate loads.

9
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,040
Don’t be mean, Liam.

10
00:00:28,607 --> 00:00:30,340
Your sister doesn’t feel great.

11
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:31,980
He’s right, Dad.

12
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:34,380
I think I was too hungry.

13
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:37,400
I didn’t have any lunch at school today.

14
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:41,800
I think you need to just go and lie down for a while.

15
00:00:42,423 --> 00:00:44,180
I’m sure you’ll feel better soon.

16
00:00:44,687 --> 00:00:45,440
OK, Dad.

17
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:46,240
I will.

18
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:48,240
I’ll just try and rest.

19
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,100
And don’t worry about the washing-up.

20
00:00:50,968 --> 00:00:52,960
I’m sure your brother will do that.

21
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:53,700
What?

22
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:54,540
Me??!!

23
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:02,360
Come in, Tim.

24
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:03,740
Take a seat.

25
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:04,740
Thank you, Doctor.

26
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:07,220
So how can I help you today?

27
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:08,660
It’s my elbow.

28
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:10,100
It’s really painful.

29
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:11,000
Look.

30
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,180
Hmm, yes, it does look a bit bruised.

31
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:18,000
So what happened?

32
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:21,040
Well, it’s a bit of a silly story really.

33
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:25,500
I got home from school yesterday and I didn’t have my key with me.

34
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:30,800
I left it in my locker at school so I tried to open the door with my elbow.

35
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,360
Oh, I see.

36
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:36,200
And it didn’t open?

37
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,260
No, it didn’t.

38
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:41,640
Well, I don’t think it’s anything too serious.

39
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:47,240
You need to put some ice on it, and take some painkillers if it hurts too much.

40
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:49,480
So, it’s not broken?

41
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,100
No, it isn’t.

42
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:54,420
You’re able to move it so I’m not too worried.

43
00:01:54,420 --> 00:02:00,220
But next time you forget your key, just wait for your parents to get home.

44
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,280
OK, Doctor.

45
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:02,180
I will.

46
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:09,820
Hello, John.

47
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:11,820
What can I do for you?

48
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:13,060
It’s my neck.

49
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,340
OK.

50
00:02:15,059 --> 00:02:17,100
And what’s the problem with it?

51
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:18,220
Does it hurt?

52
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:19,580
Yes, it does.

53
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,620
I can hardly move it.

54
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:22,380
Oh dear.

55
00:02:23,256 --> 00:02:24,240
What happened?

56
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,640
I’m not sure.

57
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:30,780
I went to bed last night and when I woke up it was really hurting.

58
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:35,520
Did you do any sport yesterday?

59
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:37,860
No, I didn’t.

60
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:41,100
But I did sleep with the window open.

61
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:46,800
My grandmother thinks the cold air made it hurt but I’m not so sure.

62
00:02:47,474 --> 00:02:50,740
No, I don’t think there’s any connection there.

63
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:55,020
OK, well, let’s have a look at it.

64
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,860
Can you take your shirt off for me, please?

65
00:02:58,460 --> 00:02:58,720
Sure.
